From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: Preserve the swapchain when image acquisition is not ready.

Marvel Rivals' launcher repeatedly recreates an unchanged 1762x833 SDR
swapchain after VK_NOT_READY on Wine-Wayland. Wine's managed child-surface
producer deliberately returns without waiting when its image ring is full,
even for an infinite acquire timeout. This avoids deadlocking synchronous
window changes against the producer thread (Wine-Wineland child-rendering
patch 0068, originally by Erhan Bilgili).

Handle this compatibility case in the presenter without adding a blocking
retry loop to Wine. Preserve the swapchain and last frame, and return the
existing no-image result to the D3D9/D3D11 callers so they can skip this
presentation attempt. A later acquire retries normally; real out-of-date,
suboptimal, resize and surface-loss handling remains unchanged. Normalize
VK_TIMEOUT to the same retry state, including after background acquisition.

Handle a transient failure on a fresh swapchain too. Previously that path
could set m_presentPending and expose an image without having acquired it,
although the caller would skip presentation, leaving future acquires stuck.

Keep the actual PresenterSync by reference while waiting on its fence.
Resetting a copy loses the fenceSignaled update and could make a retry wait
on the already-reset fence with no intervening presentation to signal it.

This is tolerance for Wine's early acquire return, not a change to Vulkan's
timeout contract. No game-specific configuration, Wine-Wayland driver
changes, forced HDR changes or overlay changes are needed.

Runtime validation pending a rebuilt DXVK: launcher startup/idle, resizing,
minimize/restore, navigation and game launch. VK_NOT_READY should no longer
cause repeated swapchain recreation. The separate DOOM native Vulkan fix
is unaffected.
---
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_presenter.cpp
@@ -98,8 +98,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
     updateSwapChain();
 
     // Don't acquire if we already did so after present
-    if (m_acquireStatus == VK_NOT_READY && m_swapchain) {
-      PresenterSync sync = m_semaphores.at(m_frameIndex);
+    if ((m_acquireStatus == VK_NOT_READY || m_acquireStatus == VK_TIMEOUT) && m_swapchain) {
+      PresenterSync& sync = m_semaphores.at(m_frameIndex);
 
       waitForSwapchainFence(sync);
 
@@ -108,6 +108,13 @@ namespace dxvk {
         sync.acquire, VK_NULL_HANDLE, &m_imageIndex);
     }
 
+    // Wine's managed child surfaces can return early to avoid blocking window
+    // updates. Keep the last frame and let the caller retry without recreating.
+    if (m_swapchain && (m_acquireStatus == VK_NOT_READY || m_acquireStatus == VK_TIMEOUT)) {
+      m_acquireStatus = VK_NOT_READY;
+      return VK_NOT_READY;
+    }
+
     // This is a normal occurence, but may be useful for
     // debugging purposes in case WSI goes wrong somehow.
     if (m_acquireStatus != VK_SUCCESS && m_swapchain)
@@ -125,12 +132,19 @@ namespace dxvk {
       if (vr != VK_SUCCESS)
         return softError(vr);
 
-      PresenterSync sync = m_semaphores.at(m_frameIndex);
+      PresenterSync& sync = m_semaphores.at(m_frameIndex);
 
       m_acquireStatus = m_vkd->vkAcquireNextImageKHR(m_vkd->device(),
         m_swapchain, std::numeric_limits<uint64_t>::max(),
         sync.acquire, VK_NULL_HANDLE, &m_imageIndex);
 
+      // A fresh swapchain can also be temporarily unavailable. Do not expose
+      // an image or set m_presentPending until acquisition actually succeeds.
+      if (m_acquireStatus == VK_NOT_READY || m_acquireStatus == VK_TIMEOUT) {
+        m_acquireStatus = VK_NOT_READY;
+        return VK_NOT_READY;
+      }
+
       if (m_acquireStatus < 0) {
         Logger::info(str::format("Presenter: Got ", m_acquireStatus, " from fresh swapchain"));
         return softError(m_acquireStatus);
